WEBVTT

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:05.440
Chikusei-so

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:21.410
<b>4/29  

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:00.970
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.120
He's late, isn't he?

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.380
Thanks for waiting.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:33.780
Are you trying to kill us?!

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.890
I was nervous since it'd been a while.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:40.690
I think changing lanes had my heart
pounding harder than the meet.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.390
What's wrong? Get in.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.780
There's not much time.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:47.310
Haiji, are you driving us there?

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:48.850
That was my intention.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.960
Isn't there anyone else here who can drive?!

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.780
Come on! Get in.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.930
What's wrong with you guys?!

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.050
I've got mine.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.050
Hurry up and get your licenses!

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.420
Yeah, you, too.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:06.830
<b><i>Bear Your Fangs at the Summit</i></b>

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:09.790
<b>Tokyo Sport University</b>

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.820
Are you okay, Prince?

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:16.210
That took longer than expected.

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:18.510
I'll check us in.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:20.610
Everyone else get ready.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:25.000
How can he say that after driving like he did?

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:30.140
One of us needs to get a license
before we train anymore.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.270
Does anyone have a plastic bag?!

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.820
Just stick it into some bushes.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.540
We can't do that!

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.000
Where's the bathroom?

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.200
I see the friendly jogging
club is as lively as ever.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.310
<i>Sakaki.</i>

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:45.850
What's up?

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.660
That's him.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:50.680
My high school teammate.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:52.620
That one, huh?

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:56.580
Prince, you okay?

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:58.800
One of you is dropping out already?

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.840
I guess it beats running.

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:03.550
After all, you'll only embarrass yourselves.

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:11.680
What? You got a problem?

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:13.690
Or...

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:18.440
Sorry, but—

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:19.330
Kiyose?

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:26.950
Kiyose!

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.930
Fujioka.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:30.910
Shit!

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:32.880
It's Rikudo University.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:34.780
Who's he?

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:39.710
It's been a while.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:42.220
Yeah. I didn't think I'd see you.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.260
Are you running?

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.380
Of course.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:48.850
You're better now?

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:51.030
Finally.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.960
Oh, sorry for interrupting your conversation.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.810
It's fine...

00:04:58.810 --> 00:04:59.960
5000m, right?

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:00.730
Yeah.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.130
I'm excited.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:03.180
It's really him...

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:02.950
Later.

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:03.690
Yeah.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:11.410
What army are they part of?

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:14.660
Rikudo University
Fourth-year Fujioka Kazuma.

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:16.580
Remember that name.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.670
Sorry, but we've got to get ready.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.210
You must be busy, too...

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:24.570
with your chores.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:36.570
Hey, don't just stand there! Move, move!

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:37.850
Yes, sir!

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:45.280
<b>Tokyo Sport University</b>

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:45.280
<b>Athletic Field</b>

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.370
Wow!

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:08.180
It's like we're a real track team!

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.420
We <i>are</i> a real track team!

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:10.680
Oh, right!

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.200
This is so amazing!

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.970
Let's get changed and start warming up.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:16.880
Time's a-wastin'.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.020
Whoa!

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:21.240
These are surprisingly cool!

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.980
Let's take a photo!

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:26.790
I'm freezing. These don't cover much.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.650
Isn't yours a little small?

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:32.610
I'm just big.

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:40.630
You're as good as they are, Musa.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:43.710
This is upsetting. This is truly upsetting.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.260
I have no redeeming qualities.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:51.620
They've surely come to Japan
in order to devote their lives to running.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.470
Their hunger is different.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:56.780
I can't possibly beat them!

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:58.890
Jota, you look sweet.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:00.330
Yeah.

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:02.440
Hey, Musa's in some weird mode.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.200
You're right. Musa's making a weird face.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:06.200
What? Let me see.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:07.080
Look at this!

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:08.630
His eyes are sticking out!

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.750
I'm surprised you can read manga right now.

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:16.370
It's to lift my spirits.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:19.770
Now is the time to lift my spirits.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:22.290
The stories I write are perfect.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.330
In my mind, anyway.

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:28.260
I knew it.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:32.220
That guy won Section Two last year.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:37.300
Champion of Hakone and captain of
the Rikudo University team, Fujioka Kazuma.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:40.670
He's been a key member of Rikudo's
Hakone Ekiden team three years in a row.

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:43.690
He's the pinnacle of college running.

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:45.290
Wow!

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.900
What? You mean Haiji knows that guy?

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:50.130
I suppose that's what this means.

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:54.620
Wow! There's a crazy number
of people on the roadside.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.050
Which section do you want to run?

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:01.250
I have no idea.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.480
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.480
Take a picture with us.

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:08.710
I'm good. Let's just get this over with.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:13.130
It's okay. You can totally beat them.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.030
Hey!

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:20.800
I've got your number tags, guys.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.020
Let's head to the track after we get these on.

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:25.390
Huh? What's wrong?

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:26.780
Nothing.

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:42.060
Whoops.

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:43.540
Sorry.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:48.070
He's the pinnacle of college running.

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:52.780
Nothing.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:02.720
<b>Tokyo Sport University</b>

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:03.500
<i>All athletes participating in the 5000m race,</i>

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:06.630
<i>please gather in front of Gate 1.</i>

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:08.400
<i>Once again,</i>

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:11.570
<i>all athletes participating in the 5000m race,</i>

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.990
<i>please gather in front of Gate 1.</i>

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:26.040
It's true that we need official records,

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.990
but first, I want you to feel
what it means to race.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:31.620
We don't have that kind of time.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:36.840
It's your first race. Let's all have fun.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.090
Let's go.

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:40.310
Oh, right.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.510
The mountains of Hakone are?

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:51.260
The steepest in the world! Let's go!

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:54.090
Someone answer him.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:03.290
Have fun? Aren't you being naïve?

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:07.580
Sorry, but today, I'll be watching to see...

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:10.290
just how well the others can run.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:29.270
Hello.

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:32.860
On your marks!

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:56.910
On your marks!

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:15.020
What's your problem?

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:34.500
Wow! He ran ahead.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.710
Boso Uni's Manas, right?

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:40.670
Guys get drawn ahead by 
his speed and screw up their pace.

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:42.720
The group's starting to stretch out.

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:53.000
<i>Do you not need to?</i>

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:57.690
Reality is harsher than that, right?

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:19.300
Someone's catching up on the outside.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:20.810
What university is he from?

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:22.930
I don't recognize his uniform.

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:26.370
Says he's from Kansei Uni.

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:34.350
Hey, there's another one!

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:40.730
No, he's being lapped!

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:42.190
You can't be serious!

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:44.310
It's only the second lap!

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:46.060
He's from Kansei Uni, too.

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:47.980
They've got a crazy lineup.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:23.250
Hey, he caught up!

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:24.070
Wow!

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:53.040
They're neck and neck!

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:55.350
Is he challenging Manas?!

00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:00.280
It's too soon!

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:03.770
They've got two more laps. Is he suicidal?

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:15.200
<i>He's on another level.</i>

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:31.160
Are you all right?

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:32.470
Would you like to drop out?

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:36.850
Here. You're dehydrated, right?

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:39.270
This is how I always run.

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:40.770
What?

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:46.740
I'm not a hamster.

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:52.660
Why do I keep running around
and around and around and...

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:07.510
<i>Is this all?</i>

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:10.960
<i>I can do it.</i>

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:21.940
<i>He can go faster?</i>

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.060
<i>Don't lose your form.</i>

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:30.570
<i>Speed up your rotations.</i>

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:32.820
<i>Faster!</i>

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.890
It's Fujioka!

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:02.770
He's coming! He's coming!

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:06.830
He's five meters ahead!

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:08.190
You can do it!

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:09.900
Last lap!

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:24.930
Last!

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:26.350
Lap!

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:49.840
Manas is getting ahead!

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:51.110
Fujioka!

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:55.990
Go!

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:53.240
Are you sure you didn't finish too quickly?

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.820
You've gotta hold back a little.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:57.020
I'm just getting started.

00:17:57.020 --> 00:17:58.100
When's your next race?

00:17:58.100 --> 00:17:59.640
I'm focusing on intercollegiate races.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.350
I'll be skipping future meets.

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:04.800
Now that's some composure.

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:06.180
We're looking forward to it.

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:07.990
Thank you.

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:21.670
Kurahara Kakeru.

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:25.960
I remember that name.

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:28.720
There was a fast runner
at a high school in Sendai.

00:18:28.720 --> 00:18:30.040
That must've been you.

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:34.230
It's an interesting team.
One Kiyose would put together.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:37.290
Last spurt! Dig deep!

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:39.670
Watch out for him.

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:40.470
What?

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:42.350
On Kiyose.

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:46.020
In top condition, he's better than that.

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:49.730
Lead the team with him.

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:52.720
With him?

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:56.440
Aren't you going for Hakone?

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:24.140
Good job, guys. You did well.

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:30.190
Musa, Joji, and Jota finished 
around seventeen minutes.

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:32.530
Shindo and Yuki finished 
around eighteen minutes.

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:35.970
Once you're used to races,
you'll reach sixteen minutes eventually.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:40.960
Nico-chan Senpai and King,
it's well within your grasp, too.

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:43.320
You shouldn't be disappointed.

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:45.990
What about this guy, then?

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:49.450
Not a single other person
finished in thirty minutes.

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:53.170
They nearly forced him to stop running.

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:58.780
No one except Kakeru and Haiji
achieved an official record.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:00.880
It's like we can't compete with them.

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:06.510
That Tokyo Sport Uni guy called us stupid.

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:10.560
Where's their sportsmanship?

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:14.240
Well, this is reality.

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:15.900
We knew this.

00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:21.780
We knew all of this.

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:25.440
Why do you care? You met the goal.

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:26.410
Yeah.

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:29.870
It doesn't matter how good my time is!

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.080
How many times do I have to say it?!

00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:37.680
Kakeru.

00:22:40.490 --> 00:22:42.590
Next time: "Dangerous Character."

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:45.840
<b>Next time: Dangerous Character</b>
